# <type>(<scope>): <emoji> <description>
#
# <optional body — explain the what and why, not the how>
#
# Verified-by: ESLint <N> errors, vitest <N> passed
# Refs: #<issue>
# Closes: #<issue>
# Co-authored-by: <name> <email>
#
# ── Types ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# feat      ✨  new feature or user-visible change
# fix       🐛  bug fix
# refactor  ♻️  rewrite/restructure, no behavior change
# perf      ⚡️  performance improvement
# docs      📝  documentation (README, CLAUDE.md, comments)
# style     💄  formatting only, no logic change
# test      ✅  add/fix tests (vitest)
# build     📦  dependencies, build config (vite, nuxt.config.ts)
# ci        👷  CI/CD pipelines (.github/workflows/)
# chore     🔧  misc maintenance/config, everything else
# revert    ⏪  revert a previous commit
# security  🔒  fix that closes a vulnerability
#
# ── Rules ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# - description: in English, imperative present tense ("add", not
#   "added"/"adds"), lowercase, no trailing period, ≤ 72 chars
# - scope: REQUIRED — lowercase area touched (e.g. footer, hero, nav,
#   i18n, deploy, ci, config, seo, icons, blog, projects), not an
#   issue number
# - emoji: optional but recommended, right after the colon
# - body: optional, wrap at ~72 chars, blank line before it
# - Verified-by: fill in real counts from `npm run lint` / `npm run
#   test` output — never write 0 without having run the command
# - Refs / Closes: optional, GitHub issue number
# - Co-authored-by: optional, delete if unused
